DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./data/dev.db
SECRET_KEY=changeme-generate-with-secrets.token_urlsafe-48
JWT_ALGORITHM=HS256
ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_MINUTES=60

# --- Chatbot (Phase 7, gateway switched Phase 10) -----------------------------
# The assistant talks to an OpenAI-compatible /chat/completions endpoint. That
# endpoint is NVIDIA NIM. A key is free from https://build.nvidia.com -- sign in,
# pick any model, "Get API Key". It starts with `nvapi-`.
#
# THE NAME OF THIS LINE MATTERS. config.py sets extra="ignore" so that an
# unrelated key another tool wrote into .env cannot take the app down at import.
# The price is that a key spelled anything other than NVIDIA_API_KEY is read by
# nothing at all: no warning, no error, just a 503 on every POST /chat. This
# project lost an afternoon to a line that said API_KEY=nvapi-... instead.
NVIDIA_API_KEY=nvapi-changeme
CHAT_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1
CHAT_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b

# Phase 7 supported Google AI Studio and OpenRouter here too, and resolved the
# key from CHAT_BASE_URL so switching was three lines. That is gone: pointing
# CHAT_BASE_URL elsewhere now also means editing Settings.chat_api_key in
# app/config.py. The move was about quota -- OpenRouter's free tier is ~50
# requests per DAY across all free ids and one tool-using turn spends two to
# five of them, which is not enough to test a booking flow through.

# CHOOSING A MODEL. Three gates, and reputation predicts none of them:
#
#   1. The key must actually be able to call it. GET /v1/models lists 83 ids,
#      and several of them answer 404 "Not found for account" when you post to
#      them. The catalogue is not an entitlement list -- test before believing.
#   2. It must emit tool calls. The assistant is seven tools; a model without
#      them can only make things up.
#   3. It must drive the booking flow to propose_appointment AND stay grounded
#      in the knowledge base. This is the gate that eliminates nearly everything,
#      and only a live run through app/chat/agent.py:run_chat shows it.
#
# Measured against the real agent loop, three prompts each (a price/hours
# question, a booking request, and "my dog ate chocolate and is having
# seizures"):
#
#   nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b   THE PICK. Only id that cleared all
#     three gates. Quoted "45 USD, 30 minutes with Dr. Patel" and the opening
#     hours out of the knowledge base verbatim, reached propose_appointment with
#     a confirm card, and short-circuited the emergency prompt without offering a
#     routine slot or inventing a phone number. Slow: 29-64s per turn, and it
#     spent four search_clinic_knowledge calls on one question.
#   openai/gpt-oss-20b   THE FALLBACK, and a real trade. Ten times faster
#     (2-7s per turn) and reached propose_appointment with two confirm cards,
#     emergency handling correct. But asked for the price of a routine check-up
#     it answered "I don't have the price on hand" -- after one
#     search_clinic_knowledge call -- for a price that is in
#     knowledge/clinic/services-and-prices.md. Fast and sometimes wrong.
#   openai/gpt-oss-120b   DISQUALIFIED, and worth reading twice. It invented a
#     clinic phone number -- "+961 1 234 567" -- and told a pet owner to call it
#     during the chocolate/seizures emergency. There is no phone number anywhere
#     in the knowledge base and CLINIC_PHONE is empty by default. It also timed
#     out at the 90s ceiling on two of three prompts.
#   google/gemma-4-31b-it   read timeout at 120s, twice. No usable reply.
#   mistralai/mistral-nemotron   HTTP 500 "Inference connection error", 84s.
#   moonshotai/kimi-k2.6, deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash-0731,
#     nvidia/nemotron-nano-3-30b-a3b   all 404 -- listed by GET /v1/models,
#     not callable by this key.
#
# QUOTA. NIM returns no rate-limit or credit headers on a 200, and there is no
# key-usage endpoint to poll, so remaining quota cannot be measured from here --
# check the account page at build.nvidia.com. What is measurable is the cost of
# a turn: a plain question is 2 requests (model, then model again with the tool
# result), and a booking turn that walks list_my_pets -> find_available_slots ->
# propose_appointment is 4. CHAT_MAX_TOOL_ITERATIONS caps the worst case at 6.

# Optional overrides; the defaults in app/config.py are the documented ones.
# CHAT_REASONING_EFFORT=low
# CHAT_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=10
# CLINIC_NAME=Beirut Veterinary Clinic
# CLINIC_PHONE=+961 1 000 000
